        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-28T05:10:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>After I game I had today, I saw another idea for a Limited variant.</p><p>Tempy had Electrical Storm out first, and one in hand. Then, The Final Wasteland played Ancient Library. Normally, if you try to play a another Limited card, the seocnd card gets destroyed. After this game though, I was considering changing it so that the 1st card gets destroyed. This would add a little bit more control over which card came out first. If the second one stayed in play, it would have let me trigger Ancient Library first, and then hit the new target with Electrical Storm. But, alas, I played by the rules. I am wondering if the rules were set up this way purposely to prevent this.</p>",
